        "math_academy_id": "q-82017",
        "problem": "If $\\overset{\u2015}{C}={3.1,4.3,5.1,7.7,9.5}$ and $\\overset{\u2015}{D}={1.8,2.7,4.3,7.7},$ then what is $\\overset{\u2015}{C\\cup D}?$",
        "worked_solution": "De Morgan's law for unions states that\n\n$$\n\\overset{\u2015}{C\\cup D}\u2261\\overset{\u2015}{C}\\cap \\overset{\u2015}{D}.\n$$\n\nSo, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\u2015}{C\\cup D} & =\\overset{\u2015}{C}\\cap \\overset{\u2015}{D} \\\\  & ={3.1,4.3,5.1,7.7,9.5}\\cap {1.8,2.7,4.3,7.7} \\\\  & ={4.3,7.7}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
